  "migration_plan": {
    "phase_1": "Create M_VFX_Universal_Translucent by duplicating M_Niagara_MelodiaFlipbook and adding the new parameter groups (DepthFade, CameraFade, Noise, Secondary, UV manipulation, static switches, SDF composite). Keep all existing params intact for backward compat.",
    "phase_2": "Create M_VFX_Universal_Masked by duplicating M_Niagara_Morning_PetalCard and applying the same parameter philosophy (color, rim, depth fade, noise, MPC).",
    "phase_3": "Create one MI per existing NS system, pointing at the universal master. Use the niagara_query set_renderer_material action. Batch via a script.",
    "phase_4": "Audit all instances: verify no default materials remain, verify Fix-A invariants (SubUV disabled, SubImageSize 1x1), verify no double-scrub.",
    "phase_5": "Retire redundant masters (mark deprecated, redirect consumers). Never cold-delete.",
    "backward_compat": "Keep M_Niagara_MelodiaFlipbook as a redirect to M_VFX_Universal_Translucent (or keep it as-is for existing instances). New instances use the universal master."
  },
  "what_makes_it_universal": [
    "1. Static switches make features optional at compile time (flipbook, rim, depth fade, camera fade, noise, beat pulse, SDF, trail, distortion, bloom, DOF, interaction, layering, temporal) — unused features cost zero.",
    "2. All parameters have sensible defaults — a bare instance renders correctly without configuration.",
    "3. Particle color is always multiplied — works for any Niagara renderer that provides particle color.",
    "4. Texture is a parameter — any texture can be assigned per instance.",
    "5. UV manipulation (tiling, pan, rotation) covers 90% of texture variation needs.",
    "6. Rim lighting is configurable (color, power, width, bias, clamp, intensity) and can be disabled (intensity=0 or static switch).",
    "7. Depth fade + camera fade handle soft intersection and distance culling.",
    "8. Noise adds distortion for mist/fire/energy without a separate material.",
    "9. Beat pulse (MPC read) enables audio-reactive effects on any instance.",
    "10. Two-sided unlit translucent base is the right foundation for 80% of VFX.",
    "11. SDF composite mode allows any instance to use SDF shapes (portal, glitter, rune, musical notation, orrery, harmonic iris) as overlays, primary shapes, or glow — without a separate material.",
    "12. Masked/lit variant covers the remaining 20% (petals, cards, solid VFX).",
    "13. AAA params (trail, distortion, bloom, DOF, interaction, layering, temporal) bring gacha-level quality.",
    "14. SDF-themed params (musical notation, orrery rings, harmonic iris) are Melodia-specific and map to the project's musical/cymatic identity."
  ],
  "what_cannot_be_universal": [
    "Blend mode (translucent vs masked vs additive) — compile-time, requires separate masters.",
    "Shading model (unlit vs default-lit vs subsurface) — compile-time.",
    "Material domain (surface vs post-process vs decal) — compile-time.",
    "Raymarched SDF as primary shape (use SDF_CompositeMode=1, but the HLSL is in the master, not a separate asset).",
    "Additive blending — if needed, create M_VFX_Universal_Additive (same graph, blend=BLEND_Additive)."
  ],
  "aaa_gacha_research": {
